  "body": "Soak up the truly magnificent views from this elevated sixth floor apartment in the much admired, mid-century Devon Park complex. Designed by renowned architect Neville Price in the 1960s, these apartments offer a sense of space, style & sophistication with expansive floor to ceiling windows that frame the ever-changing Waitemata Harbour.  From sunrise to the glittering evening lights, the panorama is nothing short of mesmerising.\r\n\r\nThis light-filled apartment features open plan living, two bedrooms – with a shared balcony, two bathrooms, and a position that’s perfect for watching the sun set over the Harbour Bridge. New carpet and a neutral décor throughout offer a comfortable feel, with scope to personalise and add value over time.\r\n\r\nSet on an acre of private landscaped grounds, Devon Park residents enjoy a solar heated pool, mature gardens, access to a private jetty, onsite live-in manager, and a peaceful, resort style atmosphere just minutes from Devonport village, all a mere 12-minute ferry ride to downtown Auckland.\r\n\r\nHomes in Devon Park are tightly held — a testament to the lifestyle, architecture, and breath-taking views. This is a rare opportunity to secure an elevated apartment on Stanley Point’s coveted waterfront — a serene, stylish retreat that offers a private sanctuary in one of Auckland’s most desirable coastal communities.\r\n\r\nPlease contact Helen on 021 210 3228 or Mel on 027 518 5424 to arrange an appointment to view.\r\n\r\n***NOTE: This property has been virtually staged***",
